Z||000003||mrgone||06-10-2001||05:49 PM||||so what do i use to get the filler plug thingy off?||||reg||1
Z||000004||johnt671||06-10-2001||06:25 PM||||Use a 10 mm socket on the bolt and loosen it so you can move the bracket that goes onto the slot on the vss.  Disconnect the wire connection to the vss. (Do this first)  Then slowly and gently pull up on the vss and it should come out.  the speedo gear is smaller than the hole for it and other than a little resistance when you first pull up it should come out easily. Slow and easy does it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||06-11-2001||02:31 AM||||Be careful NOT to let the gear fall off into the transmission!<BR>Use a flat tiped screw driver in the slot that the retainer came out of and pry up while wriggling it. Do this GENTLY! and SLOWLY!. The speedo gears have a nasty habbit of falling off and if it does you have a slim chance in HE _ _ of retrieving it! When you are pry, keep your hand over it (and in contact with it) so it won't POP out all of a sudden and strip the gear off the shaft.||||reg||1
